REVIEWED CHANGE REQUESTED (one small file, no training logic): the repository needs a single preparation script, `tools/setup_env.py`, because the unmodified code cannot start in a fresh stage container without it (details and exact code below). It is invoked by the stage `setup` and performs only file placement; every training stage is then a bare, unmodified invocation of the repo's own entry point `graphsaint.pytorch_version.train` with `--data_prefix data/<dataset>` exactly as in the README. Its content (verified to run correctly in this image) is:

#!/usr/bin/env python
import glob, os, shutil, sys
REPO = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
DATA_SRC = "/cache/data"; EXT_SRC = "/cache/data/gs_build"; DATASETS = ("ppi", "flickr")
def main():
    pkg = os.path.join(REPO, "graphsaint")
    sos = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(EXT_SRC, "*.so")))
    if len(sos) != 3:
        print("[setup_env] ERROR: expected 3 prebuilt extensions, got %d" % len(sos)); return 1
    for so in sos:
        dst = os.path.join(pkg, os.path.basename(so))
        if not os.path.exists(dst): shutil.copyfile(so, dst)
        print("[setup_env] extension ready:", dst)
    for ds in DATASETS:
        src = os.path.join(DATA_SRC, ds); dst = os.path.join(REPO, "data", ds)
        os.makedirs(dst, exist_ok=True)
        for name in sorted(os.listdir(src)):
            d = os.path.join(dst, name)
            if not os.path.exists(d): shutil.copyfile(os.path.join(src, name), d)
        print("[setup_env] data ready:", dst, sorted(os.listdir(dst)))
    return 0
if __name__ == "__main__": sys.exit(main())

Why it is unavoidable: (1) graphsaint/graph_samplers.py and graphsaint/pytorch_version/minibatch.py import graphsaint.cython_sampler / cython_utils / norm_aggr unconditionally, but the image has no C/C++ compiler and no make, and package mirrors are blocked for network stages, so `python graphsaint/setup.py build_ext --inplace` can never succeed; the prebuilt cpython-311 objects the environment engineer left in /cache/data/gs_build must simply be copied into the package (the setup script checks there are exactly 3). (2) graphsaint/utils.py loads './{prefix}/adj_full.npz', so an absolute /cache prefix is turned into the invalid path './/cache/...'; the fetched datasets must therefore be materialised under <repo>/data/<dataset> (README layout) before training. Both outputs are declared in the setup stage's `persist` and are restored for each training stage, so no stage needs a shell command of its own.

Fidelity = full: the paper's protocol runs unmodified (PPI: 1000 epochs, dim 512, arch 1-0-1-0, num_root 3000 / size_subg_edge 4000 / size_subgraph 8000, sample_coverage 50; Flickr: 15 epochs for edge/rw/mrw and 30 for node, dim 256, arch 1-1-0, sample_coverage 25). Measured with these exact commands on a T4: PPI-RW 500 s wall -> test F1-micro 0.9815 (paper 0.981±0.004); PPI-Node 389 s -> 0.9660 (0.960±0.001); Flickr-RW 17 s -> 0.5098/0.5072 (0.511±0.001); Flickr-Node 18 s -> 0.5010 (0.507±0.001). Worst case = sum of timeouts 900 + 4x1800 + 4x600 = 10500 s, of which the GPU part is 9600 s = $1.57 at T4 $0.59/h - well inside $4.98 - so no epochs, data or model size are reduced and absolute F1 values are the target. Each claim is one independent end-to-end run of one documented sampler/dataset config (the repo has no seeding code, so a run is stochastic; reported paper std is 0.000-0.007); the parsed value is the last "Full test stats: F1_Micro" line, printed after the model with the best validation F1-micro is restored. Datasets come from the paper's Google Drive folder as direct per-file downloads (drive.usercontent.google.com returns raw bytes for all 10 files, including the 357 MB flickr/feats.npy; already pre-populated so the fetch step is idempotent). No cross-stage needs other than setup->train.
